The evidence points to one main fault and one secondary fault. I'm writing up the findings.

```json
{
  "root_causes": [
    {
      "service": "search",
      "fault_kind": "network_delay",
      "evidence": [
        {"kind": "trace", "sql": "SELECT s.time s_time, s.duration/1e6 s_ms, c.time c_time, c.duration/1e6 c_ms, epoch_ms(c.time)-epoch_ms(s.time) start_gap_ms, (epoch_ms(s.time)+s.duration/1e6) - (epoch_ms(c.time)+c.duration/1e6) end_gap_ms FROM abnormal_traces s JOIN abnormal_traces c ON c.parent_span_id = s.span_id AND c.trace_id = s.trace_id WHERE s.service_name='search' AND c.service_name='rate' ORDER BY s.time LIMIT 25", "claim": "search's client span to rate lasts about 1.9 s, but rate's server span starts about 1.7 s later and runs under 1 ms."},
        {"kind": "trace", "sql": "SELECT service_name, span_name, count(*) n, approx_quantile(duration,0.95)/1e6 p95_ms, avg(duration)/1e6 avg_ms FROM abnormal_traces WHERE service_name IN ('rate','search') GROUP BY 1,2 ORDER BY 1,2", "claim": "rate's own GetRates p95 is about 1 ms, while search's rate.Rate/GetRates client span p95 is about 2.7 s."},
        {"kind": "trace", "sql": "SELECT s.service_name, s.span_name, c.service_name child_svc, count(*) n, avg(s.duration)/1e6 parent_ms, avg(c.duration)/1e6 child_ms FROM abnormal_traces s JOIN abnormal_traces c ON c.parent_span_id = s.span_id AND c.trace_id = s.trace_id WHERE s.service_name='frontend' AND c.service_name='search' GROUP BY 1,2,3", "claim": "frontend-to-search spans match in duration (about 1.9 s each), so the delay is not on the frontend-search hop."}
      ]
    },
    {
      "service": "reservation",
      "fault_kind": "container_cpu_saturated",
      "evidence": [
        {"kind": "metric", "sql": "SELECT service_name, attr_k8s_pod_name, metric, count(*) n, round(min(value),3) mn, round(max(value),3) mx, round(avg(value),3) av FROM abnormal_metrics WHERE service_name='reservation' AND metric='container.cpu.usage' GROUP BY 1,2,3", "claim": "reservation container CPU usage averages 3.3 cores in the abnormal period, versus about 0.006 normally."},
        {"kind": "trace", "sql": "SELECT span_name, count(*) n, approx_quantile(duration,0.95)/1e6 p95_ms FROM abnormal_traces WHERE service_name='reservation' GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 1", "claim": "reservation's internal memcached spans slow modestly, with reserve lookups p95 rising from about 0.64 ms to 0.95 ms."}
      ]
    }
  ],
  "propagation": [
    {"from": "search", "to": "frontend", "evidence": [{"kind": "trace", "sql": "SELECT s.service_name, s.span_name, c.service_name child_svc, count(*) n, avg(s.duration)/1e6 parent_ms, avg(c.duration)/1e6 child_ms FROM abnormal_traces s JOIN abnormal_traces c ON c.parent_span_id = s.span_id AND c.trace_id = s.trace_id WHERE s.service_name='frontend' AND c.service_name='search' GROUP BY 1,2,3", "claim": "frontend's search.Search/Nearby spans take about 1.9 s, matching search's server-side Nearby spans, so the slowdown passes up to frontend."}]},
    {"from": "reservation", "to": "frontend", "evidence": [{"kind": "trace", "sql": "SELECT service_name, span_name, count(*) n, approx_quantile(duration,0.95)/1e6 p95_ms FROM abnormal_traces WHERE service_name='frontend' AND span_name='reservation.Reservation/CheckAvailability' GROUP BY 1,2", "claim": "frontend's CheckAvailability calls to reservation rise to about 2.9 ms p95, from about 2.1 ms normally."}]}
  ]
}
```

